      "suggested_caption": "Top row: where each arm sits. Per-case scores with cohort means and 95\\% intervals. The shaded rows are supervised SCALE REFERENCES. They differ from the semi-supervised arms in labelled-case count, fold membership and training protocol at once, so the distance to them is not a label-efficiency measurement and no equivalence is claimed. Bottom row: paired per-case difference from the same no-consistency comparator, on the held-out test cohort. Points are cases, squares are means with 95\\% intervals, and the fraction at the right of each row is the number of cases favouring that arm. The two objectives are NOT weight-matched: the voxel-MSE arm shown runs at $w_{\\max}=an unrecorded weight$ against $w_{\\max}=0.10$ for soft-clDice, so it bounds rather than isolates the effect of the objective's geometry."
